-- Migration 5: retire BleAdvertisementRecord.
--
-- Superseded by BeaconObservationRecord (added in migration 4), which differs in three ways that
-- matter: it is keyed by lab session rather than by quest id, it carries the monotonic clock
-- alongside the wall clock, and it stores the anchor's surveyed iBeacon identity (uuid/major/minor)
-- instead of a device name. Name-based identity is unreadable by a backgrounded iOS app, which is
-- why the old table could not simply be extended.
--
-- No data is migrated: the old rows carry no monotonic timestamps and no anchor identity, so they
-- cannot be placed on a shared timeline and are not usable as measurements.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS BleAdvertisementRecord;
